<article class="work">
  <p>
    <em>Ayahuasca Science Mapping</em> is an experiment in organizing knowledge
    with the help of artificial intelligence. The corpus of scientific papers on
    Ayahuasca was compiled by toxicology expert Laurent Rivier.
  </p>

  <p>
    Originally brought on to evaluate the site's mockups and offer
    recommendations, I proposed building an interactive prototype to test the
    project. From there, I went on to collaborate closely on the final design.
  </p>
  <p>Avec <a href="https://www.laurentbolli.com">Laurent Bolli</a></p>
  <div class="image-bloc">
    <figure>
      <img src="images/Ayahuasca-Home.jpg" />
      <figcaption>
        The homepage encourages exploration and offers a figurative summary of
        the content.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <div class="image-bloc">
    <figure>
      <img src="images/Ayahuasca-Visualisation-Papers.jpg" />
      <figcaption>
        Scientific papers are grouped using a machine-learning algorithm.￼
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <div class="image-bloc">
    <figure>
      <img src="images/Ayahuasca-Visualisation-Authors.jpg" />
      <figcaption>
        Authors mapped according to their bibliographic proximity.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <div class="image-bloc">
    <figure>
      <img src="images/Ayahuasca-Abstract.jpg" />
      <figcaption>
        Abstracts are available along with a link to the full text.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <div class="image-bloc">
    <figure>
      <video
        id="video"
        src="images/Ayahuasca-Explore-Interaction.mp4"
        poster="images/Ayahuasca-Explore-Interaction-Poster.jpg"
        class="proto-video-X"
        playsinline
        preload
      ></video>
      <!-- Video Controls -->
      <div id="video-controls">
        <button type="button" id="play-pause">▷ Play</button>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        Several prototypes like this one were needed before landing on the most
        engaging interaction.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</article>
